Source: xorg-server-legacy-nvidia-@XABI@
Section: non-free/x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: nvidia-legacy CI <ci@nvidia-legacy.invalid>
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 pkg-config, xutils-dev, x11proto-dev,
 libx11-dev, libxext-dev, libxfont-dev | libxfont2-dev, libxkbfile-dev,
 libpixman-1-dev, libpciaccess-dev, libgl-dev, libegl-dev,
 libudev-dev, libselinux1-dev, libaudit-dev, libdbus-1-dev,
 libssl-dev, libtirpc-dev, libbsd-dev,
 flex, bison, xz-utils,
Rules-Requires-Root: binary-targets
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/kami911/nvidia-legacy

Package: xorg-server-legacy-nvidia-@XABI@
Architecture: amd64 i386
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, nvidia-legacy-xserver-common
Recommends: nvidia-legacy-@SERVES@-driver
Description: private Xorg @XVER@ (video ABI @XABI@) for legacy NVIDIA blobs
 A co-installable build of xorg-server @XVER@, installed under
 /opt/nvidia-legacy/xserver-@XABI@/ and launched only via the
 "Xorg (NVIDIA legacy)" login session. It provides X server video driver ABI
 @XABI@, which the NVIDIA @SERVES@ nvidia_drv.so needs and which the
 distribution X server (a much newer ABI) does not offer.
 .
 The distribution's own Xorg, Wayland and all other sessions are untouched.
 .
 SECURITY: an old X server receives no upstream fixes and is a larger attack
 surface. Local-session CVEs are backported in debian/patches/@XVER@/security/.
 Use only where the hardware leaves no alternative; prefer an isolated machine.

Package: nvidia-legacy-xserver-common
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: launcher + session for the private legacy NVIDIA X servers
 The nvidia-legacy-xserver wrapper, the Xsession glue and the
 "Xorg (NVIDIA legacy)" desktop-session file shared by every
 xorg-server-legacy-nvidia-* package.
